<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Farced Glorias</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">Middle Ages</span><span class="sg-chain-h">expanded text with added phrases, many in honour of the Virgin Mary</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Allein Gott in der Höh sei Ehr</span><span class="sg-chain-h">German paraphrase (early Lutheran hymn), often set to music</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria in excelsis Deo, BWV 191 (Johann Sebastian Bach)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria, RV 589 and RV 588 (Antonio Vivaldi)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">settings</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (George Frideric Handel)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting for soprano and strings, rediscovered in 2001</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (Camille Saint-Saëns)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (Francis Poulenc)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (William Walton)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (John Rutter)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (Mike Anderson)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gloria (Karl Jenkins)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting with other texts interpolated</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ich lobe meinen Gott, der aus der Tiefe mich holt</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1979</span><span class="sg-chain-h">free German paraphrase (Neues Geistliches Lied)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ich lobe meinen Gott von ganzem Herzen</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1979</span><span class="sg-chain-h">free German paraphrase (Neues Geistliches Lied)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Angels We Have Heard on High</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Christmas carol using the hymn's opening as its refrain</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">5 Star Crest (4 Vattenrum) (Bladee and Ecco2k)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">opening phrase quoted</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gospel of Luke 2:14, the angels' song to the shepherds</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the opening words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ancient Jewish liturgy</span><span class="sg-chain-h">linked to the verse in Luke by David Flusser</span></li></ul></section>
